     Screens the uninstall-protection guard covers while the settings lock is on: the system's
     device-admin screen, where protection can be deactivated. Each target is an exact package and
     a fragment of the activity class name.

     Manufacturers rename these screens. To find the right names on a phone, use the foreground
     diagnostic in a test build (Settings > Uninstall protection), open the device-admin screen for
     this app, and read off the package and class it shows.

     Note: the class name does not say WHICH admin app is being shown, so while the guard is
     active the device-admin screen of every app is covered.
-->
<guard-targets>
    <!-- Stock Android (AOSP / Pixel): Settings > Security > Device admin apps > (app). -->
    <target package="com.android.settings" class-contains="DeviceAdminAdd" />
</guard-targets>
